WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.976
From 381 down to 41.

00:00:03.076 --> 00:00:05.189
September 3, 1929:

00:00:05.199 --> 00:00:08.990
the Dow closed at a record 381.

00:00:09.097 --> 00:00:11.000
Many people had bought those shares with

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.087
borrowed money.

00:00:12.097 --> 00:00:14.612
Then, over two days, Black Monday and

00:00:14.622 --> 00:00:17.499
Black Tuesday, it lost almost a quarter

00:00:17.509 --> 00:00:18.569
of its value.

00:00:18.579 --> 00:00:20.966
And it kept sliding:

00:00:20.976 --> 00:00:24.111
by July 1932 it was down 89%,

00:00:24.121 --> 00:00:24.870
at 41.

00:00:25.002 --> 00:00:26.392
So how long did it take to

00:00:26.402 --> 00:00:27.456
climb back?

00:00:27.466 --> 00:00:28.888
Twenty-five years.

00:00:28.898 --> 00:00:31.751
It didn't close above that peak until

00:00:31.761 --> 00:00:33.056
November 1954.
